comment.narrative:
Same data maintained. 
The key elements of a functional internal quality assurance unit are defined as follows: (i) number of staff working in Quality Committees (CQ) within the university trained in internal quality standards according to national and international good practices and (ii) drafting of a reference manual/guide to internal quality assurance based on national standards and good practices. All universities have staff working in the QCs.&nbsp;

They have all been trained and certified. 9 universities have adopted their reference manual. A new detailed survey on internal quality assurance will be conducted in 1rst quarter of 2024 and will allow drawing up an updated and complete list of activities implemented by internal quality assurance units.
